Privacy Policy
Egg to Empire: Burger Tycoon · Vainsteel Studios · Last updated: 2026
Short version. This game has no accounts and no sign-up. We do not collect your name, email address or phone number. Your progress is saved on your device. Ads and in-app purchases are handled by third parties (ad networks and Google Play), which process limited technical data under their own policies.
1. Who we are
Egg to Empire: Burger Tycoon  is developed and published by Vainsteel Studios. Contact details are listed on the game's Google Play store page.

2. Information stored on your device
The game saves your progress locally on your device using standard app storage. This includes:

game state — coins, gems, buildings, upgrades, recipes, research, branches, achievements;
preferences — language, sound and music settings;
purchase flags — whether you own Remove Ads or the Supporter Pack.
This data stays on your device. We do not upload it, and we cannot read it. Uninstalling the app, or using Settings → Reset Game, deletes it permanently. There is no cloud backup, so a reset or uninstall cannot be undone by us.

3. Advertising
The free version of the game shows ads supplied by third-party advertising networks. To serve and measure those ads, the networks may process:

your device's advertising identifier;
coarse technical information such as device model, operating system version, language and approximate region;
your IP address;
interaction data such as whether an ad was shown, viewed or clicked.
We do not receive, store or sell this data. It is processed by the ad network under its own privacy policy. You can reset or limit your advertising identifier in your device settings at any time.

Purchasing Remove Ads or the Supporter Pack disables interstitial advertising. Optional reward features that previously required watching an ad continue to work, and simply grant the reward without showing one.

4. In-app purchases
Purchases are processed entirely by Google Play Billing. We never see or store your payment card, billing address or Google account details. Google Play returns to the game only a confirmation of whether a purchase completed successfully, which the game records locally as a purchase flag.

5. Permissions
The game requires internet access to load ads and to verify purchases. It does not request access to your contacts, camera, microphone, photos, precise location or files.

6. Children
This game is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided personal information to a third party through this app, please contact us and we will help you raise it with the relevant provider.

7. Data retention and your choices
Because we hold no personal data on our own servers, there is nothing for us to retain, export or erase on your behalf. You remain in full control:

Erase your game data — use Settings → Reset Game, or uninstall the app.
Limit ad personalisation — reset or opt out of the advertising identifier in your device settings.
Stop ads entirely — purchase Remove Ads or the Supporter Pack.
8. Changes to this policy
If this policy changes, the updated version will be published at this address and the "last updated" date above will change. Significant changes will also be noted in the app's store listing.

9. Contact
For any question about this policy or about your data, contact Vainsteel Studios at the email address shown on the Google Play store listing for this game.
